  "constraints": [
    {
      "text": "Minimum supported core runtime: GNU Emacs 30.1.",
      "adr": "ADR-0008"
    },
    {
      "text": "First exercised host: native Windows Emacs 31.1, with GUI and daemon/terminal checks kept distinct.",
      "adr": "ADR-0008"
    },
    {
      "text": "Initial Meow compatibility target: installed Meow snapshot 20260714.1200. Record its source revision before standalone release; do not invent an upstream tag for this snapshot.",
      "adr": "ADR-0008"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meow owns editing grammar, selection, grabs, Beacon and states. UwUmacs owns its keymaps, registry, menu labels and compatibility hooks.",
      "adr": "ADR-0002"
    },
    {
      "text": "UwUmacs core has no package manager, network access, machine paths, fonts, themes or `lem-*` dependencies.",
      "adr": "ADR-0002"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keep PowerShell default, MSYS2 explicit, language-server startup opt-in and the independent notes vault untouched.",
      "adr": "ADR-0010"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preserve the current completion stack and the frames-only preference. Frames-only is a host-selected adapter, not a mandatory dependency of core.",
      "adr": "ADR-0010"
    },
    {
      "text": "Every runtime change is authored in literate Org and tangled; generated Lisp remains tracked. Startup never tangles.",
      "adr": "ADR-0009"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keep generated files directly in `lambda-library/lambda-user/` initially. The current tangle validator rejects nested outputs; this design does not weaken that boundary.",
      "adr": "ADR-0009"
    },
    {
      "text": "Do not modify installed files under `var/elpa/`. Preserve Lambda provenance and existing licenses.",
      "adr": "ADR-0010"
    },
    {
      "text": "User overrides win deterministically. Re-enabling a mode or reloading an adapter must not duplicate bindings, hooks, advice or formatters.",
      "adr": "ADR-0005"
    },
    {
      "text": "Package integrations are selected explicitly. Loading core must not force every selected target package to load.",
      "adr": "ADR-0006"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temporary input interfaces retain control. UwUmacs must not globally commandeer minibuffers, Transient, query-replace, isearch or terminal character input.",
      "adr": "ADR-0004"
    }
  ]
}
